<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Maseca cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Maseca cut.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Smith Barney analysts Francisco Chevez and George Monserrat on Wednesday cut their rating for Mexico's Grupo Industrial Maseca SA de CV to neutral from buy.</p>
<p>-- The cut was made &quot;due to the prospect of substantially lower sales volume growth in 1997,&quot; they wrote in a report.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Maseca's sales volume is constrained by a monthly corn flour sales volume quota imposed by the Mexican government.&quot;</p>
<p>-- American Depositary Receipts in the company opened down 1/2 to 16-5/8.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
